
# Backend Documentation

The backend is a Node.js and Express REST API. It reads and writes to a SQLite database file stored on disk. All responses are JSON.

**Server file:** `backend/index.js`
**Database seeder:** `backend/init-db.js`
**Database file:** `backend/data/gadget-store.db`
**Runs on:** `http://localhost:5000`

 Starting Up

When you run `pnpm start`, the server does this before taking any requests:

1. Checks if `data/gadget-store.db` exists. If it does not, it prints an error and stops. You need to run `pnpm run init-db` first.
2. Connects to the database and turns on foreign key enforcement.
3. Makes sure the `cart_items` table exists (other tables are created by `init-db.js`).
4. Starts listening on port 5000.

Database Tables
users
Stores registered accounts.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|--------|--------|--------|
| `id` | INTEGER | Primary key, auto-increments |
| `username` | TEXT | Must be unique |
| `password_hash` | TEXT | bcrypt hash — raw password is never saved |
| `email` | TEXT | Must be unique |

products
Stores the product catalogue. Seeded with 87 products by `init-db.js`.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|--------|--------|--------|
| `id` | TEXT | Primary key, e.g. `PRD-001` |
| `name` | TEXT | Product name |
| `brand` | TEXT | Brand name |
| `category` | TEXT | One of the 5 top-level categories |
| `subCategory` | TEXT | One of the 14 subcategories |
| `price` | REAL | Stored in kobo — e.g. `1199990` means ₦11,999.90 |
| `originalPrice` | REAL | Optional. Used to show a strikethrough "was" price |
| `rating` | REAL | Out of 5 |
| `reviewCount` | INTEGER | Number of reviews |
| `description` | TEXT | Full description |
| `isFeatured` | INTEGER | 1 = featured, 0 = not |
| `isNewArrival` | INTEGER | 1 = new arrival, 0 = not |
| `tags` | TEXT | Comma-separated keywords |
| `specs` | TEXT | JSON string of key/value spec pairs |
| `stock` | INTEGER | Available units — reduced when an order is placed |
| `image_url` | TEXT | Product image URL |

**Categories and subcategories:**

| Category | Subcategories |
|--------|--------|
| Mobile & Wearables | Smartphones, Tablets, Smartwatches, Audio |
| Computing & Gaming | Laptops, Desktop PCs, Gaming, Accessories |
| Home Entertainment | Televisions, Home Theater, Streaming |
| Smart Home & Photography | Cameras, Smart Home, Office |
| Miscellaneous | Wishlist Items, Featured Deals |

 `orders`

One row per completed order.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|--------|--------|--------|
| `id` | INTEGER | Primary key, auto-increments |
| `user_id` | INTEGER | Links to `users.id`. Set to NULL if user is deleted |
| `total` | REAL | Total price in kobo |
| `date` | TEXT | Set automatically to current date and time |

 `order_items`

One row per product in an order. The price is saved at the time of purchase so it never changes.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|--------|--------|--------|
| `id` | INTEGER | Primary key, auto-increments |
| `order_id` | INTEGER | Links to `orders.id`. Deleted when order is deleted |
| `product_id` | TEXT | Links to `products.id` |
| `quantity` | INTEGER | Units purchased |
| `price_at_purchase` | REAL | Price per unit at time of order |

cart_items

Stores each user's active cart. Only one row is allowed per product per user — adding the same product again increases the quantity instead.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | INTEGER | Primary key, auto-increments |
| `user_id` | INTEGER | Links to `users.id`. Deleted when user is deleted |
| `product_id` | TEXT | Links to `products.id`. Deleted when product is deleted |
| `quantity` | INTEGER | Must be greater than 0 |
| `updated_at` | TEXT | Updated automatically on every change |


